# CI-installed native clients

<!-- Generated by make deps-sync; edit tools/depsync/native-inventory.md.in. -->

Current runner-installed client pins are generated from their executable setup
files. A new pin requires passing native CI before it is qualified. The workflow
verifies the direct client
archive or wheel before installation and prints its version where the client
offers a version command. Dockerfile clients are inventoried separately in
the client image inventory tracked by #852.

| Client and CI setup | Current version | Release and digest source | Architecture and consuming evidence |
|---|---|---|---|
| [crane](../../.github/actions/registry-clients/action.yml) | {{crane}} | [go-containerregistry releases](https://github.com/google/go-containerregistry/releases/tag/v{{crane}}), release asset SHA-256 | Linux amd64; `@docker`, `@oci` |
| [ORAS](../../.github/actions/registry-clients/action.yml) | {{oras}} | [ORAS release](https://github.com/oras-project/oras/releases/tag/v{{oras}}), release asset SHA-256 | Linux amd64; `@oci` |
| [Cosign](../../.github/actions/registry-clients/action.yml) | {{cosign}} | [Cosign release](https://github.com/sigstore/cosign/releases/tag/v{{cosign}}), release asset SHA-256 | Linux amd64; `@oci` signatures |
| [Helm](../../.github/actions/registry-clients/action.yml) | {{helm}} | [Helm release](https://github.com/helm/helm/releases/tag/v{{helm}}), official archive SHA-256 | Linux amd64; `@helm` |
| [Terraform](../../deploy/check.sh) | {{terraform}} | [HashiCorp release](https://releases.hashicorp.com/terraform/{{terraform}}/), published SHA256SUMS | Linux and macOS, amd64 and arm64; `@terraform`, provider conformance, deployment and platform scenarios |
| [Terraform null provider](../../.github/actions/registry-clients/action.yml) | {{null-provider}} | [HashiCorp release](https://releases.hashicorp.com/terraform-provider-null/{{null-provider}}/), published SHA256SUMS | Linux amd64; `@terraform_providers` |
| [JFrog CLI](../../.github/actions/jfrog-cli/action.yml) | {{jfrog}} | [JFrog CLI release](https://github.com/jfrog/jfrog-cli/releases/tag/v{{jfrog}}), [JFrog Artifactory storage checksum](https://releases.jfrog.io/artifactory/api/storage/jfrog-cli/v2-jf/{{jfrog}}/jfrog-cli-linux-amd64/jf) | Linux amd64; `@jf`, NuGet and platform scenarios |
| [Agent Package Manager](../../.github/actions/apm-client/action.yml) | {{apm}} | [APM release](https://github.com/microsoft/apm/releases/tag/v{{apm}}), release asset SHA-256 | Linux amd64; `@agentpackages` |
| [Hex Editor VSIX](../../.github/actions/ai-editor-assets/action.yml) | {{hexeditor}} | [extension changelog](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-hexeditor/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md), Marketplace manifest, VSIX and signature SHA-256 | VS Code Marketplace assets; `@aieditor` |
| [Hugging Face Hub and hf-xet](../../.github/workflows/quality-gate.yml) | {{hf-hub}} and {{hf-xet}} | [Hub files](https://pypi.org/project/huggingface-hub/{{hf-hub}}/#files), [Xet files](https://pypi.org/project/hf-xet/{{hf-xet}}/#files), PyPI wheel SHA-256 | Linux amd64, Python 3.12; `@huggingface` |
| [Conan 2 and Conan 1](../../.github/workflows/quality-gate.yml) | {{conan2}} and {{conan1}} | [Conan 2 files](https://pypi.org/project/conan/{{conan2}}/#files), [Conan 1 files](https://pypi.org/project/conan/{{conan1}}/#files), direct distribution SHA-256 | Linux amd64, Python 3.12; `@conan`; Conan 1 is the explicit legacy compatibility lane alongside Conan 2 |

The Artifactory and Platform provider conformance runner in
[`test/terraform/run.sh`](../../test/terraform/run.sh) pins the current JFrog
provider releases, {{artifactory-provider}} and {{platform-provider}}, to their checked archives. Those are
provider fixtures rather than package managers. The remaining
[`deploy/check.sh`](../../deploy/check.sh) tools are deployment checks:
TFLint {{tflint}}, Trivy {{trivy}} and terraform-docs {{terraform-docs}}. Their four-platform
archives are checksum verified too.

The current Hub client revealed a commit-response defect. [#858](https://github.com/weaveplatform/artifactweave/issues/858)
was fixed in merged [PR #859](https://github.com/weaveplatform/artifactweave/pull/859).
Hub 2.3 then passed the real model/dataset scenarios locally on merged main. The
current-client run on merged main belongs to [QUAL-01 #792](https://github.com/weaveplatform/artifactweave/issues/792).
